{"raw": {"https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/160775": {"title": "Director of Alumnae Engagement", "description": "Director of Alumnae Engagement You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Alumnae Engagement Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders.\u00a0 Salem Academy is a boarding and day college preparatory school with a focus on interdisciplinary learning using STEAM, wellness and leadership. Position Summary The Director of Alumnae Engagement is responsible for implementing a comprehensive engagement strategy and programming for alumnae in support of Salem Academy and College\u2019s overall mission. The Director of Alumnae Engagement performs the day-to-day operations of alumnae communications and the planning and execution of programs including regional events, Reunion Weekend, Academy Alumnae Board and College Alumnae Board meetings, and alumnae networking events (both virtual and in person). The Director of Alumnae Engagement assists with annual giving and Reunion giving activities as needed.\u00a0 In addition to day-to-day operations, this role will work to create and implement initiatives and programs designed to increase engagement among the 15,000+ alumnae and between the alumnae population and the institution. The Director of Alumnae Engagement will work closely with the VP of Strategic Initiatives and members of the Institutional Advancement staff to ensure that the goals of the Office of Institutional Advancement and the overall institutional goals are met. The position requires in-person work in the office and the ability to travel and work evenings and weekends, as needed. Duties and Responsibilities Plan and coordinate all aspects of the Academy and College Reunion Weekend.\u00a0 Supervise all events, recruit and work with class leaders, and maintain frequent contact to ensure attendance, class giving, and participation in Reunion Weekend events. Plan and coordinate all aspects of alumnae events, both in-person regional events and virtual events such as the bi-annual State of Salem webinars and the virtual book club. Build and manage online event invitations and registration forms in Constant Contact and through Blackbaud NXT. Coordinate and manage the Academy Alumnae Board and the College Alumnae Board to ensure appropriate leadership is in place.\u00a0 Serve as the principal staff liaison to the board for purposes of fulfilling the goals of the institution. Work in cooperation with Institutional Advancement and Marketing & Communications to develop content for publications, marketing materials, alumnae newsletters, etc. Collaborate with Marketing & Communications to develop a bi-monthly News from the May Dell newsletter geared towards alumnae population. Work with the Marketing & Communications to keep the alumnae web pages (Academy and College) and all institutional social media outlets up-to-date with news, events, and other marketing \u2013 Instagram, Facebook, etc. Maintain the official alumnae social media accounts and serves as an administrator (along with several alumnae volunteers) of the \u201cunofficial\u201d social media accounts (Academy and College) Educate graduating students about alumnae benefits and engage them in alumnae programs Support Alumnae Awards Committees that publicly recognize outstanding alumnae leaders and Nominating Committees to bring diverse representation of our alumnae populations into the Alumnae Boards Foster strong relationships with various constituencies of the Academy and College by responding to inquiries, both verbal and written, directed to the alumnae office regarding a variety of issues and concerns including the status or location of graduates, affiliation procedures and policies, upcoming alumnae activities and events, or other associated matters Lead Reunion Class Officer training and coordinate with 80 class officers, who change annually, on a regular basis throughout the Reunion cycle Coordinate the scope of work in collaboration with other IA staff members to maximize efficiencies. Evaluate and implement ways to streamline processes Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s Degree Three to five years of related professional experience to include work in fundraising, planning and managing special events, identifying, training and working with volunteers, preferably in a higher education setting Highly proficient computer skills Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with a broad range of internal and external constituents including faculty, staff, students, alumnae, parents, donors, volunteers, and friends of the Academy and College Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively through the development and composition of professional correspondence and formal presentations Strong interpersonal skills Ability to effectively multi-task and produce accurate professional work products under demanding timelines Ability to establish cooperative, effective working relationships Outstanding planning and organizational skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively Proven ability to display discretion in dealing with sensitive, confidential issue s Sound judgment and problem-solving skills Ability to travel and to work evenings and weekends as needed Preferred Qualifications Prior experience with development or fundraising software; Volunteer recruitment and management experience. Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Director of Alumnae Engagement, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem Academy and College is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law in its employment practices. For questions, contact Katherine Knapp Watts, Vice President of Strategic Initiatives at katherine.watts@salem.edu Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162190": {"title": "ERP Administrator Ellucian Colleague", "description": "ERP Administrator Ellucian Colleague You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account ERP Administrator Ellucian Colleague Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Position Summary This position serves as the College's primary administrator for the Ellucian Colleague ERP platform. The ERP Administrator leads day-to-day administration, configuration, security, reporting, integrations, and operational support of the ERP throughout implementation and post-go-live operations. In keeping with the needs of a small private college, the role also supports enterprise applications, business intelligence, automation, and strategic technology initiatives outside the ERP ecosystem. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Serve as the primary technical and functional administrator for Ellucian Colleague. Support ERP implementation, testing, data validation, cutover, and stabilization. Administer security roles, upgrades, patches, integrations, and scheduled processes. Develop reports, dashboards, SQL queries, and data extracts. Maintain ERP documentation, procedures, and knowledge articles. Partner with functional offices to improve business processes and data quality. Coordinate with Ellucian and third-party vendors. Provide Tier II/III support and end-user training. Secondary Enterprise Responsibilities: Support Microsoft 365, SharePoint Online, Entra ID, and Power Platform solutions. Assist with SaaS application administration and identity management. Develop workflow automations and support API integrations. Participate in data governance, disaster recovery, software lifecycle, and technology projects. Assist with IT asset management and documentation. Qualifications Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Business Information Systems, or related field, or equivalent experience. Three or more years supporting enterprise applications. Strong analytical, customer service, communication, and documentation skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience administering Ellucian Colleague. Experience participating in an ERP implementation or major ERP upgrade. Higher education experience. Experience with SQL Server, Power BI, Microsoft 365, Entra ID, SharePoint Online, APIs, and Ellucian Ethos. ITIL Foundation and/or project management experience . Core Competencies Business Process Analysis Problem Solving Relationship Building Customer Service Project Coordination Continuous Improvement Communication Adaptability Performance Expectations (First 12 Months) Support a successful Colleague implementation and post-go-live stabilization. Reduce ERP support issues through proactive administration and documentation. Implement meaningful dashboards and operational reporting. Develop standardized procedures for ERP administration. Identify automation and process improvement opportunities. Become the trusted technology partner for academic and administrative departments. While performing the responsibilities of the ERP Administrator (Ellucian Colleague), the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; routinely stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Must be able to travel with students and staff throughout the campus. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. For questions, please contact Garth Cromier, chief information officer at garth.cromier@salem.edu or JaNae Joyner, chief operating officer at janae.joyner@salem.edu Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162186": {"title": "Maintenance Technician II HVAC", "description": "Maintenance Technician II HVAC You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Maintenance Technician II HVAC Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country. Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. POSITION SUMMARY Under the general direction of the Executive Director of Operations, as an essential employee, the Maintenance Technician II HVAC reports directly to the Assistant Director of Facilities. The position is responsible for maintaining and repairing all types of commercial and residential HVAC-R equipment, monitoring automated control systems, changing filters and belts, cleaning drains, working with high and low-voltage wiring, working with control wiring, troubleshooting any HVAC-R equipment, working to establish a preventative maintenance schedule/system for all HVAC-R equipment. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Responsible for maintaining the buildings and related equipment in a timely, efficient, and professional manner. Must be knowle dgeable in general building maintenance, HVAC-R, plumbing, electrical, and carpentry. Such as HVAC-R, boilers, chillers, and pumps. Provide & respond to maintenance, repair and work order requests Performs maintenance duties, maintenance functions specific to the assigned facilities and/or based on needs for seasonal/project requirements. Assists with managing inventory of maintenance supplies. Drives vehicles required to perform or travel to maintenance work, including Salem vehicles, vans, or industrial equipment. Reports needs and concerns to supervisor/appropriate staff, which may include submitting or recommending work orders and checking supply levels within on-campus buildings and residence halls, responsible for reporting concerns related to on-campus residents. Ensure proper care in the use and maintenance of equipment and supplies; promotes continuous improvement of workplace safety and environmental practices. Assists in on-the-job training of new staff on routine procedures. Ability to work rotating shifts, weekends, holidays, during inclement weather, and during other circumstances requiring maintenance staffing. Assist with the snow removal as needed Performs other tasks, duties, and responsibilities as assigned. POSITION KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES Strong understanding of general maintenance processes and methods. Ability to understand and follow safety procedures. Ability to safely use maintenance equipment and supplies. Ability to lift and manipulate heavy objects up to 60lbs Excellent communication, oral, interpersonal, and writing skills. Strong troubleshooting skills Work independently with demonstrated problem-solving skills. Knowledge of general maintenance best practices, procedures, and terms associated with building maintenance, and physical plant operations. Knowledge of inventory control practices. Ability to establish and maintain an effective working relationship between diverse operating groups, personnel, and organizations. Ability to perform repetitive motion for long periods of time. Excellent manual dexterity, innovative/critical thinking, and problem-solving skills Demonstrate proficiency with technology, computers, and computerized maintenance management system (CMMS). Qualifications Required Qualifications Must hold universal CFC certification. Minimum of 5 years of HVAC experience High school diploma or equivalent Must reside within 30 minutes of campus Valid driver's license. Ability to pass a background check. Submit to random drug testing Ability to pass a fitness for duty evaluation. Physical/Environmental Requirements: Bend, squat, stand, kneel, walk, run, crawl, and climb. Regularly ascend/descend stairs. Walk for long distances and sit for varying lengths of time. Reach above shoulders, handle keys/tools/objects, push, pull, carry, or lift over 50 lbs. Work may necessitate accessing and working in confined spaces or high spaces. M ust be physically able to operate the equipment required to perform duties . Work in an indoor/outdoor environment subject to changing temperatures. Ability to lift heavy objects, climb ladders, and work at heights Considerable physical activity. Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing or pulling required objects up to 50 pounds. Physical work is a primary part (more than 70%) of the job. Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Work may involve moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises. Salem Academy and College is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law in its employment practices. For questions, please reach out to Jason Tracy at jason.tracy@salem.edu Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/165879": {"title": "Wellness and Academic Counselor", "description": "Wellness and Academic Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Wellness and Academic Counselor Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem Academy is a boarding and day college preparatory school with a focus on interdisciplinary learning using STEAM, wellness and leadership.\u00a0Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Position Summary Salem Academy seeks a dedicated and student-centered Wellness & Academic Counselor to support the academic, social-emotional, and overall well-being of Academy students. The Wellness & Academic Counselor serves as a primary resource for students experiencing mental health, social-emotional, personal, academic, organizational, or adjustment concerns that may affect their ability to thrive at Salem Academy. The counselor serves as a key liaison between the Academy, families, campus partners and outside providers to promote continuity of care and ensure students have appropriate mental health and academic support both in and outside of school. In addition to its core counseling duties, the position provides individualized academic support to students who may benefit from assistance with organization, executive functioning, study strategies, time management, self-advocacy, and understanding themselves as learners. The counselor collaborates with Academy administration, faculty and staff to identify students who may need additional academic support and to develop coordinated strategies for student success. Salem Academy and College maintains an Institutional Director of Accessibility Services serving both Salem Academy and Salem College students. That role retains primary responsibility for creating formal accommodation plans and initial family meetings related to accommodations. The Wellness & Academic Counselor contributes to the Academy's broader Wellness & Leadership mission through proactive wellness initiatives, student support programming, and collaboration with Academy administration, faculty & staff. This position is designed as the Academy\u2019s first point of contact for students experiencing mental health, social-emotional, or adjustment concerns. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Student Mental Health & Counseling The Wellness & Academic Counselor will maintain a strong and visible counseling presence within the Academy and serve as a primary resource for student mental health and social-emotional concerns. Identify student needs and coordinate appropriate care for students experiencing social-emotional, mental health, personal, academic, or adjustment concerns. Provide crisis response and initial risk assessment in accordance with school protocols, professional standards, and ethical requirements. Advocate for student well-being and help identify and reduce barriers to learning and participation. Support students in developing coping strategies, self-awareness, emotional regulation, resilience, and appropriate help-seeking behaviors. Maintain appropriate professional boundaries and recognize when a student's needs require outside or specialized clinical care. Maintain accurate and confidential counseling documentation in accordance with FERPA, professional standards, and school policy. Participate in student support meetings and contribute a mental health perspective to coordinated student support planning. Mental Health Coordination & Family Partnership The Wellness & Academic Counselor serves as a primary school liaison for coordinating student mental health support among the student, family, Academy, and outside providers. Serve as a primary point of contact for families regarding significant student mental health and social-emotional concerns. Establish collaborative relationships with parents and guardians while maintaining appropriate student confidentiality. Coordinate communication among students, families, school personnel, and outside counselors, therapists, psychologists, psychiatrists, and other mental health providers, with appropriate permissions and releases. Collaborate with outside providers, when appropriate, to understand recommendations that may affect a student's school experience and assist in translating those recommendations into appropriate school-based supports. Maintain appropriate documentation of communication and support plans while protecting student confidentiality. Academic & Learning Support The Wellness & Academic Counselor provides individualized academic support for students whose academic success may be improved through direct coaching, skill development, and increased self-awareness as learners. Provide academic coaching related to: Organization Time management Executive functioning Study strategies Test preparation Help students develop individualized strategies for managing the academic demands of a college-preparatory environment. Support students in developing self-advocacy skills and communicating appropriately with teachers and other members of their support team. Collaborate with advisors and faculty when students demonstrate patterns of academic difficulty that may benefit from additional intervention. Review relevant academic information and student progress, when appropriate, to identify students who may need additional support. Collaborate with the Institutional Director of Accessibility Services when a student's academic needs may intersect with formal accommodations or learning differences. Refer students who may benefit from an evaluation for accommodations or additional learning support to the Institutional Director of Accessibility Services. This position does not independently develop, approve, or manage formal accommodation plans. Wellness & Prevention Programming The Wellness & Academic\u00a0 Counselor contributes to the Academy's broader Wellness & Leadership focus and supports a proactive approach to student mental health. Collaborate with the Dean of Students and Wellness Committee on schoolwide wellness initiatives. Identify emerging student wellness needs and recommend appropriate programming or interventions. Conduct regular check ins with students that utilize services related to wellness & academic support Assist with faculty and staff professional development related to recognizing student mental health concerns and responding to students in distress. Promote a school culture in which seeking help is normalized and students understand how to access support. Teach wellness course programming such as study skills and social-emotional learning curriculum. Program Evaluation & Professional Practice Maintain accurate and confidential records related to counseling and student support services. Remain current on best practices in school counseling, adolescent mental health, learning support, executive functioning, and student wellness. Participate in professional development relevant to the position. Maintain appropriate professional licensure or certification. Participate in committees, school activities, and community events as appropriate to the position. Perform other duties consistent with the position as assigned by the Dean of Students or Head of School. Qualifications Required Qualifications Master's degree in School Counseling, Counseling Psychology, Social Work, or a related field. Licensure or certification as a School Counselor or equivalent credential appropriate for school-based counseling. Experience providing counseling, student support, or related services in a school or youth-serving environment. Knowledge of adolescent development and school-based mental health practices. Strong understanding of academic support strategies, executive functioning, and student self-advocacy. Strong communication, collaboration, organization, and crisis-response skills. Ability to establish trusting relationships with adolescents and their families. Ability to maintain appropriate confidentiality and professional boundaries. Preferred Qualifications Three or more years of experience working with high school students. Experience working in a boarding or residential school environment. Experience coordinating with outside mental health providers and community resources. Experience supporting students with learning differences or executive functioning Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Wellness and Academic Counselor, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. For questions, contact Nicole Gatto, Dean of Students at nicole.gatto@salem.edu Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/165947": {"title": "Public Safety Officer - Part-time", "description": "Public Safety Officer - Part-time You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Public Safety Officer - Part-time Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Job Shift 3rd Shift - 12:00 a.m. - 8:00 a.m. Education Level High School Travel Percentage Negligible Category Other Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 252-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Position Summary The Public Safety Officer is an essential employee who reports directly to the Director of Public Safety and will be responsible for all security activities involving campus patrol, requests for service, opening/closing of facilities, responding to emergency calls, parking requests, and monitoring, and all other duties as assigned. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Respond to calls for service. Communicate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and public safety departmental members regarding campus policies, procedures, emergency processes. Answer and monitor telephone and radio systems. Respond to emergency-based assignments and directives by supervisors and other institutional administrators. Work cooperatively and effectively with all members of the department, and other campus constituencies. Be familiar with, locate and communicate information in the Salem student handbooks, employee manuals, and Emergency Response Plan manual. Computer skills necessary to complete incident reports create campus identification cards, email correspondence, parking registration, payroll system, etc. Be familiar with and able to operate all fire alarm systems and burglar alarm systems on campus. Maintain current knowledge of buildings and properties including but not limited to safety hazard checks, security checks, floor plans, and employees that maintain offices in each facility. Assists with after-hour emergency facility related work as needed. Ability to work rotating shifts, weekends, holidays, during inclement weather, and during other circumstances requiring public safety staffing. Provide constant foot patrol to the entire campus. Ability to use physical force to protect yourself or others if necessary and legitimately permissible. Be familiar with and use all issued equipment as required/needed. Performs and completes any other special tasks, responsibilities, and duties as assigned. Position Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Excellent communication, oral, interpersonal, writing, and presentation skills. Knowledge of law enforcement/security best practices and procedures. Analytical skills and objective observation of situations and quick decision-making. Skill in managing situations firmly, courteously, tactfully, and impartially. De-escalation skills Ability to multi-task and work independently with demonstrated problem-solving skills. Ability to establish and maintain an effective working relationship between diverse operating organizations. Ability to organize work. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. Ability to cope with changing requirements, and goals (sometimes rapid changes). Qualifications Required Qualifications High school diploma or general education degree (GED) required Minimum of 2 years of security or law enforcement related work experience required Ability to pass a background check Working knowledge of basic security techniques Must be able to establish and maintain effective working relationships with superiors, Salem students, staff, administration, and community Subject to random drug testing Ability to pass a background check At least 21 years of age Valid driver's license Physical/Environmental Requirements: Bend, squat, stand, kneel, walk, run, crawl, and climb. Regularly ascend/descend stairs. Walk for long distances and sit for varying lengths of time. Reach above shoulders, handle keys/tools/objects, push, pull, carry, or lift objects over 40 lbs. Work may necessitate accessing and working in confined spaces or high spaces. Must be physically able to perform tasks appropriately. M ust be physically able to operate the equipment required to perform duties . Work in an indoor/outdoor environment subject to changing temperatures. Salem Academy and College is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law in its employment practices. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/170558": {"title": "Controller", "description": "Controller You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Controller Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Category Accounting Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Position Summary The Controller is a senior financial leader responsible for directing the accounting and financial reporting functions of the Academy and College while supporting the strategic financial direction of the institution. Reporting to the Vice President for Finance/Chief Financial Officer, the Controller ensures the integrity of the institution's financial records, maintains strong internal controls, and provides accurate and timely financial information to support institutional decision-making. This position provides leadership for the daily operations of the Controller\u2019s Office and oversees accounting, financial reporting, treasury management, audits, tax compliance, grants accounting, and financial systems. The Controller partners with campus leaders to develop financial strategies that support the Academy and College's mission while ensuring compliance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), federal and state regulations, donor restrictions, and institutional policies. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Controller will: Provide leadership and oversight for all accounting functions of the institution, including: General ledger Accounts payable Accounts receivable Cash receipts Payroll accounting Fixed asset accounting Capital asset accounting Month-end and year-end close processes Ensure the accuracy, completeness, and integrity of the institution's financial records while maintaining strong internal controls to safeguard institutional assets. Prepare and oversee: Monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements Financial reports for senior leadership and the Board of Trustees Budget-to-actual analyses Cash flow reports Financial forecasts and other management reports Coordinate the annual external financial audit, Single Audit and preparation of financial statements while responding to auditor requests and implementing recommendations. Assist the Vice President for Finance/CFO with: Annual operating budget development Capital budget preparation Multi-year financial forecasting Long-range financial planning Financial modeling and institutional decision support Oversee treasury management activities, including: Cash management Banking relationships Investment accounting Debt accounting Cash flow forecasting Ensure compliance with: Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) Federal and state regulations IRS reporting requirements Donor restrictions Grant requirements Debt covenant reporting Direct accounting and financial reporting for grants, endowments, restricted funds, and capital projects while ensuring compliance with funding requirements. Develop, implement, and continuously improve financial policies, procedures, and internal controls that promote efficiency, accountability, and sound financial stewardship. Provide leadership in the implementation, maintenance, and optimization of financial systems, accounting software, reporting tools, and ERP financial modules. Supervise, coach, and develop accounting staff by providing leadership, performance management, mentoring, and professional development. Partner with Human Resources regarding payroll accounting, employee benefits accounting, retirement reporting, and other employee-related financial matters. Collaborate with budget managers and departmental leaders by providing financial guidance, budget monitoring, and analysis to support sound fiscal management. Prepare financial analyses, presentations, and reports for executive leadership, Cabinet, Board committees, accreditation activities, and strategic initiatives. Monitor changes in accounting standards, regulations, and higher education financial practices and recommend improvements to ensure ongoing compliance and operational effectiveness. Serve on institutional committees and represent the Controller\u2019s Office on cross-functional initiatives and strategic planning efforts. Perform other duties as assigned by the Vice President for Finance /Chief Financial Officer. Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in accounting, Finance, or a closely related field. Minimum \u00a0of eight years of progressively responsible accounting or financial management experience. Minimum of five years of supervisory experience. Comprehensive knowledge of: Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) Financial reporting Budget development Internal controls Auditing Nonprofit accounting Demonstrated ability to analyze complex financial information and communicate financial concepts to both financial and non-financial audiences. Strong leadership, organizational, analytical, and project management skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. High level of integrity, professionalism, discretion, and commitment to confidentiality. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Thorough knowledge of nonprofit and higher education accounting principles and financial reporting requirements. Strong understanding of budgeting, treasury management, financial analysis, and internal controls. Ability to interpret complex financial information and make sound recommendations. Ability to build collaborative relationships across the institution while providing exceptional customer service. Ability to lead organizational changes, improve financial processes, and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel and financial information systems. Ability to exercise independent judgment while maintaining the highest standards of ethics, confidentiality, and stewardship of institutional resources. Preferred Qualifications Certified Public Accountant (CPA) designation preferred. Master\u2019s degree in a related field preferred. Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Controller the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem Academy and College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. For questions, please contact Darrell Farewell, Chief Financial Officer and Vice President for Finance at darrell.farewell@salem.edu Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/171973": {"title": "Part-Time Public Safety Officer", "description": "Part-Time Public Safety Officer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Part-Time Public Safety Officer Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level GED Category General Business Apply Description Position Description Position Title: Public Safety Officer Supervisor: Director of Public Safety Position Status: Part-Time / 12-Month Business Calendar Schedule Classification: Non-Exempt About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem Academy is a boarding and day college preparatory school with a focus on interdisciplinary learning using STEAM, wellness and leadership.\u00a0Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Position Summary The Public Safety Officer is an essential employee who reports directly to the Director of Public Safety and will be responsible for all security activities involving campus patrol, requests for service, opening/closing of facilities, responding to emergency calls, parking requests, and monitoring, and all other duties as assigned. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Respond to calls for service. Communicate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and public safety departmental members regarding campus policies, procedures, emergency processes. Answer and monitor telephone and radio systems. Respond to emergency-based assignments and directives by supervisors and other institutional administrators. Work cooperatively and effectively with all members of the department, and other campus constituencies. Be familiar with, locate and communicate information in the Salem student handbooks, employee manuals, and Emergency Response Plan manual. Computer skills necessary to complete incident reports create campus identification cards, email correspondence, parking registration, payroll system, etc. Be familiar with and able to operate all fire alarm systems and burglar alarm systems on campus. Maintain current knowledge of buildings and properties including but not limited to safety hazard checks, security checks, floor plans, and employees that maintain offices in each facility. Assists with after-hour emergency facility related work as needed. Ability to work rotating shifts, weekends, holidays, during inclement weather, and during other circumstances requiring public safety staffing. Provide constant foot patrol to the entire campus. Ability to use physical force to protect yourself or others if necessary and legitimately permissible. Be familiar with and use all issued equipment as required/needed. Performs and completes any other special tasks, responsibilities, and duties as assigned. Position Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Excellent communication, oral, interpersonal, writing, and presentation skills. Knowledge of law enforcement/security best practices and procedures. Analytical skills and objective observation of situations and quick decision-making. Skill in managing situations firmly, courteously, tactfully, and impartially. De-escalation skills Ability to multi-task and work independently with demonstrated problem-solving skills. Ability to establish and maintain an effective working relationship between diverse operating organizations. Ability to organize work. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. Ability to cope with changing requirements, and goals (sometimes rapid changes). Qualifications Required Qualifications High school diploma or general education degree (GED) required Ability to pass a background check Working knowledge of basic security techniques Previous security-related work experience preferred Must be able to establish and maintain effective working relationships with superiors, Salem students, staff, administration, and community At least 21 years of age Valid driver's license Physical/Environmental Requirements: Bend, squat, stand, kneel, walk, run, crawl, and climb. Regularly ascend/descend stairs. Walk for long distances and sit for varying lengths of time. Reach above shoulders, handle keys/tools/objects, push, pull, carry, or lift objects over 40 lbs. Work may necessitate accessing and working in confined spaces or high spaces. Must be physically able to perform tasks appropriately. M ust be physically able to operate the equipment required to perform duties . Work in an indoor/outdoor environment subject to changing temperatures. Salem Academy and College is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law in its employment practices. For questions, contact Karen Boyd, Chief of Public Safety at karen.boyd@salem.edu For Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/171964": {"title": "Mathematics Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Mathematics Adjunct Instructor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Mathematics Adjunct Instructor Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously-operating educational institution for girls and women in the U.S.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich, 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Job Summary: The Mathematics adjunct\u00a0instructor teaches up to two courses in the Mathematics program, preparing and delivering in-person learning activities designed to achieve course outcomes. Specifically, this position is needed to teach one or both of the following courses during the Spring 2027 semester: Elementary Functions and Graphs and Finite Mathematics. The adjunct will develop course materials including a syllabus, homework assignments, and content for the Course Management System (CMS). They will evaluate and grade students\u2019 class work, online work, assignments, and examinations and hold a minimum of two regularly-scheduled office hours per week throughout the semester.\u00a0They must maintain and submit student attendance records, grades, and other required documentation by specified deadlines, as well as prepare and maintain course materials within the Salem College CMS and communicate with enrolled students through a Salem email account. Additionally, they will participate in periodic meetings with one or more members of the Mathematics program faculty. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaches one or two courses in the Mathematics program Prepares and delivers in-person learning activities in order to achieve course outcomes Prepares course materials such as syllabi, homework assignments, and material for Course Management System (CMS) Evaluates and grades students\u2019 class work, online work, assignments, and examinations Holds a minimum of two regularly-scheduled office hours per week of classes throughout the semester Maintains and submits student attendance records, grades and other required documentation by specified deadlines Prepares and maintains course material on the Salem College CMS Communicates with enrolled students through the use of a Salem email account Participates in periodic meetings with one or more members of the Mathematics program faculty Qualifications Qualifications Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or higher in Mathematics or a related discipline with at least 18 graduate-level course hours in mathematics or related disciplines Excellent communication (verbal, written and interpersonal) and organizational skills Sensitivity to respond appropriately to the needs of the community Preferred Qualifications Prior experience teaching classes in Mathematics at the undergraduate or graduate level as instructor of record Experience in instructional technology Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, Google Workspace, or equivalent Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the course instructor, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand and walk; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation and view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in a classroom setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. For questions, contact Wade Mattox, Director of the Mathematics Program at\u00a0wade.mattox@salem.edu Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/172585": {"title": "Enterprise Applications and ERP Systems Administrator", "description": "Enterprise Applications and ERP Systems Administrator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Enterprise Applications and ERP Systems Administrator Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem Academy is a boarding and day college preparatory school with a focus on interdisciplinary learning using STEAM, wellness and leadership.\u00a0Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Position Summary The Enterprise Applications & ERP Systems Administrator is a hands-on, cross-functional technology professional responsible for the administration, integration, reporting, and operational support of Salem College's core enterprise applications, with primary responsibility for the Student Information System (SIS) and associated distributed ERP environment. The position combines ERP administration with enterprise application, database, integration, Microsoft 365, identity, automation, and technical project responsibilities. This role is designed for a small-college environment where technology staff work across traditional functional boundaries. The successful candidate will serve as a key technical resource during our future ERP/SIS implementation and stabilization period while also providing sustainable support for the College's broader enterprise application ecosystem. Essential Responsibilities ERP & Enterprise Application Administration Serve as the primary technical and functional administrator for Ellucian PowerCampus. Support ERP implementation activities including configuration support, testing, data validation, conversion, cutover, go-live, and post-implementation stabilization. Administer ERP security roles, upgrades, patches, scheduled processes, interfaces, integrations, and related operational functions. Troubleshoot complex enterprise application issues and provide Tier II/III support. Coordinate with Ellucian and other third-party vendors for support, implementation, upgrades, and issue resolution. Maintain current system documentation, operating procedures, configuration records, and knowledge articles. Provide end-user training and knowledge transfer to functional and technical staff. Data, Reporting & Database Support Develop and maintain SQL queries, reports, dashboards, data extracts, and operational reporting solutions. Support relational databases used by enterprise applications, including database troubleshooting, data validation, and appropriate administrative activities. Partner with institutional offices to improve data quality, reporting consistency, and business processes. Support data conversion, reconciliation, validation, and migration activities associated with ERP and enterprise application projects. Participate in data governance initiatives and help implement standards for institutional data quality, stewardship, access, and documentation. Integrations & Automation Design, develop, support, and troubleshoot integrations between enterprise systems using APIs, integration platforms, database methods, file exchanges, and other appropriate technologies. Support integrations involving Ellucian PowerCampus and third-party higher education platforms such as admissions/CRM (Slate), payment, learning, document, and other SaaS systems. Develop workflow automations and process improvements using Microsoft Power Platform or comparable tools. Monitor integration health, investigate failures, and maintain technical documentation for interfaces and data flows. Microsoft 365 & Enterprise Technology Support Support Microsoft 365 services, including SharePoint Online, Entra ID, and Power Platform solutions. Assist with SaaS application administration, identity and access management, and application lifecycle activities. Participate in disaster recovery, software lifecycle management, IT asset management, and other institutional technology projects. Assist with technical evaluation, implementation, documentation, and support of new enterprise applications. Project, Service & Stakeholder Responsibilities Lead or coordinate assigned technology projects and workstreams using sound project management practices. Work closely with functional offices to translate business needs into practical technical solutions. Provide responsive, customer-focused service and communicate effectively with both technical and nontechnical stakeholders. Support continuous improvement of IT service delivery, documentation, change management, and operational processes. Perform other related duties as assigned consistent with the scope and level of the position. Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in information technology, computer science, information systems, or a related field; equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience may be considered. Three or more years of experience supporting enterprise applications environments. Three or more years of database management, database development, or closely related experience, or equivalent education. Strong SQL development skills (T-SQL, PL/SQL, or comparable SQL dialects). Experience with one or more relational database platforms such as Microsoft SQL Server, Oracle, MySQL/MariaDB, or PostgreSQL. Experience integrating applications using APIs and other common integration methods. Experience with reporting/development toolsets such as Microsoft SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS), Microsoft Visual Studio, Power BI, or comparable platforms. Strong Microsoft 365 skills, particularly Excel. Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot complex application, data, and integration issues. Strong verbal, written, analytical, customer service, and documentation skills. Demonstrated project coordination or project management experience. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work effectively in a small, collaborative IT organization. Preferred Qualifications Experience administering Ellucian PowerCampus or similar SIS (Ellucian Colleague, Banner, Jenzabar, Workday, Anthology\u2026etc.). Experience participating in an ERP implementation, migration, or major ERP upgrade. Higher education technology experience. Experience with application integration platforms such as Ellucian Ethos, Constituo, MuleSoft, Boomi, or comparable tools. Experience with SQL Server, Power BI, Microsoft 365, Entra ID, SharePoint Online, and Power Platform. Python development or scripting skills. Experience supporting higher education integrations such as Slate or other admissions/CRM platforms. Familiarity with third-party payment platforms. ITIL Foundation certification and/or formal project management training or certification. Experience evaluating and applying AI-enabled tools, automation, and intelligent workflows to improve business processes, system integrations, data access, and operational efficiency, with appropriate consideration for data privacy, security, governance, and responsible AI use. Experience identifying and implementing practical AI use cases that improve connectivity between enterprise systems, reduce manual processes, enhance data quality, and improve the user experience. Position Scope This position is intentionally broad and combines responsibilities commonly distributed across an ERP Administrator and an Enterprise Applications/Integrations professional. Priorities should be managed by IT leadership to ensure that mission-critical ERP operations, integrations, security, data integrity, and implementation commitments receive appropriate focus. Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Enterprise Applications and ERP Systems Administrator the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem Academy and College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. For questions, please contact Garth Cormier, Fractional CIO at garth.cormier@salem.edu or JaNae Joyner, COO and VP of Administration and Operations at janae.joyner@salem.edu. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/172951": {"title": "Director of Public Safety", "description": "Director of Public Safety You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Public Safety Hot Job Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description About Salem Academy and College Salem Academy and College is the oldest continuously operating educational institution for girls and women in the country.\u00a0 Since 1772, the institution has engaged in transformational change to innovate women\u2019s education. Founded with the mission of making education accessible to all, Salem has a rich 254-year-old history and a long-standing track record of educating students who are prepared to make a bold impact locally, nationally and globally through liberal arts education. Our graduates are committed to making the world a better, healthier and more equitable place. Salem College is the nation\u2019s only liberal arts college exclusively dedicated to developing the next generation of health leaders. Position Summary The Director of Public Safety reports directly to the Executive Director of Operations and provides leadership for Salem\u2019s Department of Public Safety, a non-sworn, unarmed campus safety department, and has overall responsibility for administering and managing the department\u2019s short- and long-range strategic planning, personnel administration, employee development, policy creation and implementation, and general oversight of the department. Consistent with the practice at many liberal arts colleges, Salem\u2019s public safety officers do not carry firearms and do not have arrest authority; the Director builds and maintains a strong partnership with the Winston-Salem Police Department and other local law enforcement, fire, EMS, and emergency response agencies for matters requiring sworn law enforcement action, arrest authority, or criminal investigation. As an essential employee, the Director implements best practices in campus safety and community-oriented safety services; ensures compliance with federal and state laws and regulations; prepares and distributes the college\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report as required by the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Crime Statistics Act; and directs, plans, and manages all functions and operations of the Public Safety Department. The Director fosters a welcoming, service-oriented department culture that maintains a safe and secure environment on the Salem campus for students, staff, and guests. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Collaborates with the Executive Director of Operations to develop departmental advancement, capital, strategic training, campus safety, and operating plans. Directs, supervises, and evaluates departmental staff and supervisors; ensures staff receive training in customer service, de-escalation, trauma-informed response, and their specific job responsibilities. Recruits, hires, trains, and develops a team of public safety officers grounded in a community-focused, service-oriented approach to campus safety. Assists with the development of departmental budgets; orders equipment and supplies, monitors inventory, and makes requests for capital outlay expenditures as needed. Establishes department goals, long-range plans, objectives, policies, directives, and procedures based on the needs of Salem and continuously monitors and evaluates the effectiveness of the department. Establishes, maintains, reviews, and regularly updates department practices, policies, and procedures to ensure best practices are employed, consistent with a non-sworn, unarmed campus safety model. Serves as Clery Compliance Officer in partnership with Salem administration to prepare the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. Coordinates with the College Title IX Coordinator on related campus-wide training, investigations, and safety planning. Conducts regular oversight and inspection of department personnel, equipment, and operational practices, and identifies opportunities to improve department operations and the community\u2019s service experience. Ensures proper and timely notification to appropriate stakeholders and departments within the Salem community. Oversees discipline of department staff and makes recommendations on departmental disciplinary decisions. Ensures complaints against department employees are thoroughly and fairly investigated. Plans, implements, and maintains effective customer and stakeholder relations, outreach programs, and educational programming for students, staff, and faculty regarding safety, crime prevention, and risk reduction. Builds and maintains a positive, collaborative working relationship with the Winston-Salem Police Department and other outside law enforcement, fire, EMS, and first responder agencies, serving as the college\u2019s primary liaison for matters requiring sworn law enforcement response, arrest authority, or criminal investigation. Participates in community organization meetings focused on community safety and security. Oversees the security of campus buildings and property, including access control, key/card systems, and camera systems; develops contingency and emergency plans for Salem and provides safety-related guidance to senior staff. Oversees patrol of campus property by public safety officers to maintain a visible, welcoming safety presence, deter incidents, and identify hazards; ensures officers respond promptly to safety and security concerns and escalate any matter requiring law enforcement authority, arrest, or criminal investigation to the Winston-Salem Police Department or other appropriate agency. Serves as the college\u2019s primary point of contact for emergency incidents on campus, directing Salem\u2019s internal response, coordinating with campus partners, and escalating to outside law enforcement or emergency responders as needed. Serves as a member of Salem\u2019s Emergency Operations Response team and other task forces, as appointed. Maintains daily contact with internal community members (students, staff, faculty, parents, etc.) in a manner that reflects Salem\u2019s values and commitment to a caring, student-centered environment. Leads and manages the department and is ultimately responsible for its operations, performance, and culture. Provides after-hours support for emergency facility-related matters as needed. Works rotating shifts, weekends, holidays, during inclement weather, and during other circumstances requiring public safety staffing. Performs other tasks, duties, and responsibilities as assigned. Position Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent oral, written, interpersonal, and presentation communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with superiors, subordinates, Salem students, staff, faculty, administration, the surrounding community, and local law enforcement and emergency response partners. Knowledge of campus safety and security best practices within a non-sworn, unarmed public safety environment. Skill in managing situations calmly, courteously, tactfully, and impartially, with an emphasis on de-escalation and trauma-informed response. Ability to multi-task and work independently with demonstrated problem-solving skills. Ability to supervise and guide individuals or groups, balancing employee concerns with management requirements. Ability to provide constructive feedback to staff and manage disciplinary and performance issues fairly. Skilled in developing and coordinating department training programs, including customer service, de-escalation, and emergency response training. Knowledge of office administration, business operations, budgeting, and reporting. Knowledge of the legal and regulatory framework governing campus safety, including the Clery Act, Title IX, and related federal and state requirements. Ability to manage documentation and records related to safety incidents, reports, and investigations. Knowledge of purchasing and inventory control practices. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships across diverse operating units and constituencies. Ability to organize work and maintain schedules. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing, with a broad range of audiences. Ability to adapt to changing requirements, priorities, and resources, sometimes on short notice. Demonstrated ability to plan, develop, and provide collaborative leadership grounded in community trust. Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution, preferably with an emphasis in criminal justice, public administration, higher education administration, or a related field; an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience will be considered. Minimum of 7 to 10 years of progressively responsible experience in campus safety, security administration, higher education, or a related field, including supervisory or management experience; experience within a non-sworn, unarmed campus safety environment is strongly preferred. Demonstrated experience with emergency management planning, Clery Act compliance, and building collaborative partnerships with local law enforcement and emergency response agencies. Current certification, or ability to obtain within six months of hire, in CPR, First Aid, and AED. Ability to pass a background check. Subject to drug testing. Valid driver's license. Physical/Environmental Requirements: Bend, squat, stand, kneel, walk, and climb. Regularly ascend/descend stairs. Walk for long distances and sit for varying lengths of time. Reach above shoulders; handle keys, tools, and objects; push, pull, carry, or lift up to 40 lbs. Work may require accessing and working in confined or elevated spaces. Must be physically able to safely perform assigned duties and operate the equipment required for the position. Work in an indoor/outdoor environment subject to changing temperatures and weather conditions. Salem Academy and College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. For questions, please contact Tina Kramer, Executive Director of Operations at tina.kramer@salem.edu Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161075": {"title": "Student-Writing Center Tutor", "description": "Student-Writing Center Tutor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student-Writing Center Tutor Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description The Salem College Writing Center is hiring students who have completed the three semester hour internship. Responsibilities : Consult/tutor students with writing projects in person and online Log work hours in Google Drive folder Attend biweekly staff meetings Attend biweekly professional development work sessions Engage in professional development work Potential Professional Development Work : Create content for social media Run social media accounts Plan events that engage the Salem community Assist Dr. Manthey with writing center research and academic publication Create and deliver workshops on campus Curate and promote our zine library Develop materials for writing in your discipline Learning Objectives : Gain experience as a professional tutor Become familiar with best practices of writing center work Work collaboratively on professional development projects that connect to your personal career goals Requirements : Completion three semester hours of SALEM275 or ENGL211 Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161561": {"title": "Student-Admissions Student Assistant", "description": "Student-Admissions Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student-Admissions Student Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description Position Summary To aid the admissions office staff in their day-to-day activities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Answer phones in a professional manner when needed File Data Entry Write postcards Run Errands Prepare letters for mailing Greet visitors when needed Help staff prepare for visitation days Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Good office etiquette Confidentiality Honesty Dependability Basic computer skills Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Admissions Student Assistant , the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161554": {"title": "Student- Admissions Communications Team", "description": "Student- Admissions Communications Team You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student- Admissions Communications Team Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description Position Summary: To assist the Admissions Office with social media, phone calls, and emails to prospective students. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Call prospective students to notify of a visit from a Salem representative, encourage student to apply or complete their application and encourage students to attend an event Make confirmation calls for visitation events Keep neat and detailed record of calls made in Slate Use social media as instructed to reach potential students Required Qualifications: Strong telephone skills Genuine enthusiasm for Salem College Confidentiality Honesty Reliability Motivation and Initiative Evening Hours Physical Functions: While performing the responsibilities of the Admissions Communications Assistant , the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161550": {"title": "Student - Financial Aid Office Assistant", "description": "Student - Financial Aid Office Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student - Financial Aid Office Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Job Shift 1st Shift - 8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Education Level Not Specified Travel Percentage Negligible Category Education Apply Description Position Summary To assist the Financial Aid staff in their day-to-day activities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Answer student\u2019s questions when possible or direct them to the appropriate person File Distribute incoming mail Assist with mailings Run errands Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Good office etiquette Confidentiality Honesty Reliability Motivation and Initiative Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Financial Aid Student Assistant, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161546": {"title": "Student-Chemistry Lab Assistant", "description": "Student-Chemistry Lab Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student-Chemistry Lab Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description The Chemistry Lab Assistant supports the Chemistry Department by assisting faculty with the preparation, organization, and maintenance of instructional laboratories. This position provides students with valuable hands-on laboratory experience while helping ensure chemistry labs operate safely, efficiently, and in accordance with established laboratory safety standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare laboratory equipment, chemicals, glassware, and supplies for laboratory classes. Set up and clean up chemistry laboratories before and after lab sessions. Clean, organize, and properly store laboratory equipment, glassware, and chemicals. Monitor laboratory supply inventory and notify faculty when materials need to be replenished. Assist faculty with routine laboratory preparation and basic laboratory procedures. Follow all chemical hygiene and laboratory safety procedures, including the proper handling and disposal of chemical waste. Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory environment. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the Chemistry Department. Qualifications: Strong attention to detail and commitment to laboratory safety. Ability to follow written and verbal instructions and work independently. Dependable, punctual, and organized. Ability to lift and carry up to 25 pounds and stand for extended periods while performing laboratory tasks. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161540": {"title": "Student-Biology Assistant", "description": "Student-Biology Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student-Biology Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description The Biology Lab Assistant supports the Biology Department by assisting faculty with the preparation, organization, and maintenance of teaching laboratories. This position provides students with hands-on laboratory experience while helping ensure biology labs operate safely and efficiently. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare laboratory materials, specimens, and equipment for class activities. Set up and clean up biology laboratories before and after lab sessions. Clean, organize, and maintain laboratory equipment and workspaces. Monitor laboratory supply inventory and notify faculty when materials need to be replenished. Assist with basic laboratory procedures under faculty supervision. Follow laboratory safety procedures and maintain a clean, safe working environment. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the Biology Department. Qualifications: Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to follow written and verbal instructions and work independently. Dependable, punctual, and able to maintain confidentiality when appropriate. Ability to lift and carry up to 25 pounds and stand for extended periods while performing laboratory tasks. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161535": {"title": "Student Assistant- Student Center", "description": "Student Assistant- Student Center You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student Assistant- Student Center Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Education Level High School Travel Percentage None Apply Description Position Summary The Student Center Assistants support the daily operations of the Student Center by providing exceptional front-line customer service and creating a welcoming environment for students, faculty, staff, alumni, and visitors. Serving as the primary reception point for the Student Center, Office Assistants assist with guest services, facility operations, event support, equipment check-out, and building information. They also complete administrative projects and provide operational support to the Student Activities staff to ensure the smooth day-to-day functioning of the Student Center and its programs, events, and services. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide administrative support by answering phones, greeting visitors, answering routine questions to determine needed resources, make referrals, and provide information on policies, office services, and programs. Process reservations and monitor conference room usage in Student Center. Monitor and respond to posting violations involving student organizations. Provide set up for conference room space including furniture and technology assistance. Assist in the development and implementation of resources, programs, and projects for Student Activities. Assist in the compilation, design, and delivery of resource materials that support Student Activities to include media wall slides, table tents, and social media promotion. Assist staff with coordinating programs that will foster an increased sense of community among stakeholders who use the Student Center. Restock sanitary products in bathrooms regularly. Assist with the Student Activities weekly newsletter and social media posts. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Commitment to the mission of the Office of Student Affairs Excellent customer service skills and professional work habits Demonstrated ability to communicate and partner with a diverse group of stakeholders Ability to work independently and take initiative Excellent oral and written communication skills Prior experience planning and organizing meetings, events and programs Dependable and responsible Organized and able to multi-task Ability to act as a team member Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Student Center Assistant, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, squat, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 50\u00a0 pounds to 70% of the time; regularly stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; physically able to operate the equipment required to perform duties ; ability to lift heavy objects, climb ladders, and work at heights; work in an indoor/outdoor environment subject to changing temperatures; Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions; work may involve moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises, perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161528": {"title": "Student - Residence Life Campus  Assistant", "description": "Student - Residence Life Campus  Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student - Residence Life Campus  Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Education Level High School Travel Percentage None Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description Position Summary: Residence Life is responsible for providing a safe and nurturing living-learning environment for residential students. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Promoting activities through social media Assisting with lockouts Educating residents about housing procedures Covering office hours Staffing the Campus Care Hub Building community throughout the residential population Greet guests and ensure they have signed in properly Assist RA by notifying them of who is visiting in which room Manage equipment, product inventory, and check out Qualifications Required Qualifications Commitment to the mission of Residential Life Excellent customer service skills and professional work habits Demonstrated ability to communicate and partner with a diverse group of stakeholders Ability to work independently and take initiative Excellent oral and written communication skills Dependable and responsible Ability to act as a team member Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Residence Life Campus Assistant the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, squat, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 50\u00a0 pounds to 70% of the time; regularly stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; physically able to operate the equipment required to perform duties; ability to lift heavy objects, climb ladders, and work at heights; work in an indoor/outdoor environment subject to changing temperatures; Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions; work may involve moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises, perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/161522": {"title": "Student-Design and Art Lab Assistant", "description": "Student-Design and Art Lab Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student-Design and Art Lab Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description Job Summary: The Design and Art Lab Assistant will support the daily operations of the Art & Design department's labs and studios, as well as the interiors resource room and chair library. This position is ideal for students who are organized, responsible, and have an interest in maintaining a clean, safe, and productive creative environment. The assistant will help monitor lab usage, maintain equipment and materials, support lab safety protocols, and assist faculty and staff with general upkeep and organization. Key Responsibilities: Monitor student use of labs and studios to ensure proper use of tools, materials, and equipment Assist with daily cleanup procedures and encourage others to maintain shared spaces Organize supplies, tools, and materials; restock as needed Report damaged or malfunctioning equipment to faculty or lab managers Help maintain a safe and clean work environment in accordance with department and school safety policies Assist with the setup and breakdown of class or project spaces as needed Support department staff with inventory, labeling, and general organizational tasks Provide Chair library tours when requested Qualifications: Must be a current student with a valid work-study award Strong attention to detail and a proactive, responsible attitude Basic familiarity with art and design tools, equipment, or materials (training provided) Ability to work independently and follow directions Good communication skills and a willingness to assist peers and faculty Punctual and dependable Preferred (but not required): Previous experience working in studios or labs Interest in art, design, or creative disciplines Basic knowledge of safety protocols or equipment maintenance To Apply: Submit your resume and class schedule to Dr. Rosa Otero at rosa.otero@salem.edu Physical Functions This position requires the ability to perform tasks commonly associated with studio and lab maintenance. The student must be able to: Stand or walk for extended periods while monitoring labs or performing cleanup; Lift and carry up to 30 pounds (e.g., boxes of supplies, tools, or equipment); Bend, stoop, reach, and perform repetitive motions for cleaning and organizing; Use hands and fingers to handle tools, materials, and small components; Tolerate exposure to common studio materials (e.g., clay dust, paints, solvents\u2014with proper protective measures); Work in a shared environment that may involve noise, dust, and moderate physical activity. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162478": {"title": "Student - Mercantile Store Clerk", "description": "Student - Mercantile Store Clerk You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student - Mercantile Store Clerk Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level High School Category General Labor Apply Description Title: College \u2013 Mercantile Store Clerk Position Summary The Mercantile Store Clerk is responsible for assisting customers with items in the Mercantile, answering customer questions, assisting customers with purchase decisions, and completing sales transactions. They also help with checking in merchandise and restocking items in the store. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Welcoming and engaging with customers as they enter the Mercantile Assessing customers\u2019 needs and suggesting solutions to their problems Working with cash registers and processing payments Giving customers advice about sales, promotions, and recommending best products Using upselling techniques to increase store sales Assisting in maintaining and setting up merchandise displays on the sales floor Assisting with promotions, sale events, and social media posts Cleaning and restocking the store throughout the day, before opening and after closing Other duties as needed Qualifications Required Qualifications Strong customer service skills including effective communication Ability to prioritize and organize workload Ability to work independently Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Mercantile Store Clerk, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162474": {"title": "Student-Quest Tutor", "description": "Student-Quest Tutor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student-Quest Tutor Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level High School Category Education Apply Description Position Description Position Title: \u00a0Quest Tutor Position Summary: Salem College is dedicated to the academic success of its students.\u00a0 We\u2019re seeking a passionate and knowledgeable Tutor in our Quest Tutoring Program to join our team and provide personalized support to students of various ages and skill levels. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Provide one-on-one or small group tutoring sessions in various subjects, including but not limited to Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Spanish and other subjects needing support. Assess students' strengths and weaknesses to tailor lessons and improve their understanding of key concepts. Develop and implement engaging lesson plans and practice exercises that align with curriculum standards. Assist students with homework, test preparation, and project completion. Monitor and track student progress, offering constructive feedback and adjusting teaching methods as needed. Foster a positive and encouraging learning environment that builds students' confidence and enthusiasm for their subject. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Experience in relevant field demonstrated by successful completion of courses in the topic of study, recommendations from faculty of the specific discipline or equivalent experience. Proven experience as a tutor or educator, preferably with experience in the relevant subjects. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to explain complex concepts in a clear and relatable manner. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Patience, empathy, and a passion for teaching and helping students succeed Physical Functions: While performing the responsibilities of the Admissions Counselor, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 40 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, viewing computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem Academy and College is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law in its employment practices. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162470": {"title": "Student - Operations Student Worker", "description": "Student - Operations Student Worker You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student - Operations Student Worker Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level High School Travel Percentage None Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description Title: College \u2013 Operations Student Worker Student Supervisor: Executive Director of Operations Position Summary Under the general direction of the Executive Director of Operations, as an essential employee, the Operations Student Worker will be assigned to one of the four departments within Operations (Grounds, Custodial Mail Services, and Maintenance) as needed. While assigned to a department, the Operations Student Worker will report to the supervisor/lead of each respective department while performing assigned work. Once assigned, the Operations Student Operations Student Worker will commonly provide routine grounds maintenance, housekeeping, and maintenance functions and any other duties assigned. Operations Student Worker must be physically able to perform tasks appropriately. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Work cooperatively and effectively with all members of the department, and other campus constituencies. Keeps the buildings and property in clean and orderly condition. Performs essential tasks, functions and responsibilities and routine grounds, custodial, mail services and maintenance activities. Drives vehicles & small equipment required to perform or travel to the worksite. Notifies managers regarding the need for repairs or additions to buildings Reports needs and concerns to supervisor/appropriate staff, which may include submitting or recommending work orders and checking supply levels within on-campus buildings and residence halls, responsible for reporting concerns related to on-campus residents. Ensures proper care in the use and maintenance of equipment and supplies; promotes continuous improvement of workplace safety and environmental practices. May assist or perform activities and minor work, such as weeding, planting, replacing light bulbs, moving furniture, basic office & dorm room cleaning, setup/teardown of events, mail delivery and other similar activities. Ability to work rotating shifts, weekends, holidays, during inclement weather, and during other circumstances requiring operations staff. Performs other tasks, duties, and responsibilities as assigned. Qualifications Required Qualifications Valid driver's license. High school diploma or equivalent Minimal experience in operations preferred Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Operations Student Worker the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, squat, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 50\u00a0 pounds to 70% of the time; regularly stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; physically able to operate the equipment required to perform duties; ability to lift heavy objects, climb ladders, and work at heights; work in an indoor/outdoor environment subject to changing temperatures; Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions; work may involve moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises, perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162461": {"title": "Student Technical Assistant", "description": "Student Technical Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student Technical Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description This Student Technical Assistant position provides support for events by setting up and breaking down equipment, assisting with audio/visual needs, and ensuring the smooth operation of events. This position may also assist with proper set-up and arrangement of equipment, table, chairs, furniture etc. on campus as a result of events. This technical assistant may also keeps track of inventory in the building and assist with other projects deemed appropriate by the Director of Special Events and Community Outreach. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162456": {"title": "Student - Athletics Assistant", "description": "Student - Athletics Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student - Athletics Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Education Level None Travel Percentage None Category Other Apply Description Position Summary The Athletics student employment position is a role that will assist the athletic department in accomplishing functions necessary for athletic excellence. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Duties may include: office work, game management, concessions, statistics, scoreboard, assisting the athletic trainer, photography, videography, game day operations, making posters and graphics. Assignments may be placed by the director of athletics, the assistant director of athletics, the athletic trainer, the sports information director, and the coaches. There is office work as well as evening work to support the athletic home events. The work to be performed is quite diverse in nature. Attendance to assigned shifts is required.\u00a0 Two unexcused absences will result in the removal of employment.\u00a0 If a student worker will be absent from a shift, they must notify the director of athletics before the shift.\u00a0 Notification after the assigned shift will count as an unexcused absence. The student worker may be exposed to confidential information.\u00a0 This information cannot be discussed or made available to anyone without the proper approval of the director of athletics.\u00a0 Sharing confidential information with any unauthorized person is ground for immediate dismissal. Communication between the student worker and the athletics department staff is critical to job performance.\u00a0 If a problem or confusion arises, it is expected that all parties involved will work to resolve the issue. Qualifications Required Qualifications Dependable Honest Organized Enthusiastic about Salem College Athletics Evening and Weekend hours available Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Athletics Assistant , the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162450": {"title": "Student - Academy Babcock Desk Assistant", "description": "Student - Academy Babcock Desk Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student - Academy Babcock Desk Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level High School Travel Percentage None Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description Position Summary: The Academy Weekend Assistant supports the Academy Residence Life team by providing administrative assistance, maintaining an organized and welcoming environment, and assisting with student engagement initiatives, special projects, and weekend operations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assist with student check-in/check-out Answer phones in a professional manner Answer students\u2019 questions when possible or direct them to the appropriate person Maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming environment Willingness to transport and ability to drive school vehicles needed to transport students as needed Assist with planning, preparing, and executing Residence Life programs, events, and activities. Assist with creating event materials, assembling supplies, and preparing spaces before and after programs. Perform light cleaning and resetting of program spaces and other areas as needed. Demonstrate flexibility and a willingness to assist with a variety of duties that contribute to the success of the Residence Life program. Perform other duties as assigned Skills Qualifications Professional office etiquette Professional demeanor Confidentiality Honest Reliable Motivated Great communication Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Academy Assistant Swimming Coach, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem Academy and College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Qualifications Required Qualifications Professional office etiquette Professional demeanor Confidentiality Honest Reliable Motivated Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Academy Assistant Swimming Coach, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a\u00a0computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means\u00a0of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem Academy and College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162446": {"title": "Student-Library Services Student Assistant", "description": "Student-Library Services Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student-Library Services Student Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Apply Description The Library Services Student Assistant performs general and routine service desk duties by assisting library users with library resources and helping maintain library materials. This position serves as the first point of contact for library users. Primary Duties: -Greeting library users in person, answering the telephone, and responding to online chat -Checking materials in and out -Responding to library user requests -Assisting library users with basic research and directional inquiries -Conducting searches in the library catalog and databases -Locating library materials in the physical stacks and online -Assisting library users with printing and scanning -Offering referrals to Salem librarians and staff members -Assisting with closing the library during Sunday \u2013 Thursday evening shifts -Assisting Salem librarians and staff members with projects as assigned Required Qualifications: -Excellent communication skills -Enjoy helping and interacting with people -Interest in learning new research skills -Perseverance in answering questions - Ability to multitask Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F9BC0E3EF21EBFD06396ABA365BF2DCF/jobs/162442": {"title": "Student - Institutional Advancement Assistant", "description": "Student - Institutional Advancement Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student - Institutional Advancement Assistant Salem Academy and College - Winston Salem, NC 27101 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level High School Travel Percentage None Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description Position Summary: The student assistant will be an integral liaison in the Institutional Advancement Office, helping steward alumnae and donors through various communications (written and spoken) and representing our student population at alumnae/donor events, which is an essential need. The position also will assist with general administrative tasks required in the Institutional Advancement Office. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: As requested by the Office and as student\u2019s schedule allows, attend and assist with special events for alumnae and donors (ex. Regional Alumnae Events, Health Leadership Forum, Christmastide, Scholarship Luncheon, Reunion Weekend, etc) Communicate with alumnae and donors (via phone, email, video and notes) to encourage attendance at alumnae events; coordinate any special needs (ex, parking, mobility access, etc) for campus events; make phone calls to thank donors for gifts Help maintain records used by Institutional Advancement (scanning documents and attaching to donor records, filing any appropriate hard copy documents, etc) Other duties as requested and assigned through the Institutional Advancement Office Required Qualifications: Excellent verbal and written communication skills (very important!) Interest in meeting and working with alumnae and donors from various generations and geographical areas General computer skills (Google, Microsoft products) Understanding of utmost confidentiality in all aspects of work performed Physical Functions While performing the responsibilities of the Student Assistant, the employee is required to sit for varying lengths of time; bend, reach, lift, push, and pull up to 25 pounds; occasionally stand, walk, and kneel and regularly ascend/descend stairs; use hands and fingers to handle or feel and manipulate keys on a keyboard; perform extended periods of work at a computer workstation, view a computer monitor; perceive sounds at normal speaking levels with or without correction, and receive detailed information through oral communication; express and exchange ideas by means of spoken word; and work in an office setting. Salem College is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, religion, disability status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is avail